ns":["Absolute values only","Relative behaviour or growth rates near a point or infinity","The number of roots of two functions, no matter which values are selected.","The exact values at all points"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"dbeff3ef7e7550bf597ef058"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_asymptotic_equivalence_3eb0a15f_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which asymptotic equivalence is valid as $x\\to 0$?","options":["$\\sin x\\sim 1$ as $x\\to 0$","$\\ln(1+x)\\sim 1$ as $x\\to 0$","$\\sin x\\sim x$ as $x\\to 0$","$x\\sim x^2$ as $x\\to\\infty$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"77f5f70c62ca13dcdec42893"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_asymptotic_equivalence_3eb0a15f_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which logarithmic asymptotic equivalence is valid as $x\\to 0$?","options":["$\\ln(1+x)\\sim x$ as $x\\to 0$","$\\ln x\\sim x$ as $x\\to 0$","$\\mathrm{e}^x\\sim x$ as $x\\to 0$","$1+x\\sim x$ as $x\\to 0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9002459b25b718297f2cff47"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_asymptotic_equivalence_3eb0a15f_005","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which property of asymptotic equivalence is correct?","options":["It is never symmetric","It applies only to polynomials","It requires exact equality for all $x$","It is symmetric and transitive"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"c1a6fc0e5cd4808357e2b2b8"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_asymptotic_equivalence_3eb0a15f_006","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"In which kinds of limits may equivalent functions be substituted?","options":["Sums where leading terms may cancel","Limits of constant functions only","Pointwise equalities away from the limiting point","Limits involving products or quotients"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"8dbb02d0d0f80eaee49011b5"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_asymptotic_equivalence_3eb0a